  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 1004.04 Protection of Landfill Closure Systems",
  "priorExpiration": "1997-10-29",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 1004.04 Protection of Landfill Closure Systems. The design of a facility shall include measures or features to avoid damage during construction and operation of the facility to any component of a landfill closure system, including:\n\n(a) Ground control markers;\n\n(b) The capping system;\n\n(c) Leachate collection system risers and clean-outs;\n\n(d) Groundwater monitoring wells; and\n\n(e) Decomposition gas control devices.\n\nSource. #5172, eff 7-1-91; ss by #6535, INTERIM, eff 7-1-97, EXPIRES: 10-29-97; ss by #6619-B, eff 10-29-97; (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Sw 1000); ss by #8459, eff 10-28-05 (formerly Env-Wm 2704.04); ss by #10598, eff 7-1-14; ss by #13864, eff 2-6-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1000.html"
